===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|bagge}}, from {{der|en|non|baggi|t=bag, pack, satchel, bundle}} (whence also {{cog|fro|bague|t=bundle, package, sack}}); related to {{cog|non|bǫggr|t=harm, shame; load, burden}}, of {{unc|en|nocap=1}} origin. Perhaps from {{der|en|ine-pro|*bʰak-}} (compare {{cog|cy|baich|t=load, bundle}}, {{cog|grc|βάσταγμα|t=load}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|băg}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈbæɡ/}}
** {{a|Southern England|Australia}} {{IPA|en|/ˈbæːɡ/}}
** {{a|NZ|some US dialects}} {{IPA|en|/ˈbɛɡ/}}
** {{a|Upper Midwestern US}} {{IPA|en|/ˈbeɪɡ/}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-bag.ogg|Audio (US)}}
** {{audio|en|EN-AU ck1 bag.ogg|Audio (AU)}}
* {{rhymes|en|æɡ|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}
# A soft container made out of [[cloth]], [[paper]], thin [[plastic]], etc. and open at the top, used to hold food, commodities, and other goods. 
#: {{syn|en|poke|q1=obsolete|sack|tote}}
# A container made of leather, plastic, or other material, usually with a handle or handles, in which you carry personal items, or clothes or other things that you need for travelling. Includes [[shopping bag]]s, [[schoolbag]]s, [[suitcase]]s, and [[handbag]]s.
#: {{hypo|en|sack|pouch|tote|bindle|purse|backpack}}
# {{lb|en|colloquial}} One's [[preference]].
#: {{syn|en|cup of tea|thing|Thesaurus:predilection}}
#: {{ux|en|Acid House is not my '''bag''': I prefer the more traditional styles of music.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Newton Thornburg|authorlink=Newton Thornburg|title=Cutter and Bone|year=1976|publisher=Little, Brown|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/cutterbone00thor/page/250/mode/1up|isbn=978-0-316-84390-4|page=250|passage=And from then on, his '''bag''' was silence. Silence and killing.}}
# {{lb|en|derogatory}} An [[ugly]] [[woman]].
#: {{syn|en|dog|hag}}
# {{lb|en|LGBT|slang|USA|derogatory}} A fellow gay man.<ref name="Niemoeller"/>
# {{lb|en|baseball}} The cloth-covered pillow used for first, second, and third [[base]].
#: {{ux|en|The grounder hit the '''bag''' and bounced over the fielder’s head.}}
# {{lb|en|baseball}} First, second, or third [[base]].
#: {{ux|en|He headed back to the '''bag'''.}}
# {{lb|en|preceded by "the"}} A [[breathalyzer]], so named because it formerly had a plastic bag over the end to measure a set amount of breath.
# {{lb|en|mathematics}} A collection of objects, disregarding order, but (unlike a [[set]]) in which elements may be repeated.
#: {{syn|en|multiset}}
#: {{ux|en|A '''bag''' of three apples could be represented symbolically as {a,a,a}. Or, letting 'r' denote 'red apple' and 'g' denote 'green apple', then a '''bag''' of three red apples and two green apples could be denoted as {r,r,r,g,g}.}}
# A [[sac]] in animal bodies, containing some [[fluid]] or other substance.
#: {{ux|en|the '''bag''' of poison in the mouth of some serpents}}
#: {{ux|en|the '''bag''' of a cow}}
# {{lb|en|now|historical}} A [[pouch]] tied behind a man's head to hold the back-hair of a [[wig]]; a [[bag wig]].
#* {{RQ:Smollett Peregrine Pickle|volume=II|54|passage=[H]e had once lost his '''bag''', and a considerable quantity of hair, which had been cut off by some rascal in his passage through Ludgate, during the lord mayor's procession.}}
#*'''1774''', {{w|Frances Burney}}, ''Journals & Letters'', Penguin 2001, 1 December:
#*:He had on a suit of Manchester velvet, Lined with white satten, a '''''Bag''''', lace Ruffles, and a very handsome sword which the King had given to him.
# The quantity of [[game]] bagged in a [[hunt]].
# {{lb|en|slang|vulgar}} The [[scrotum]].
# {{lb|en|UK}} A unit of measure of [[cement]] equal to 94 pounds.
# {{lb|en|mostly|in the plural}} A dark [[circle]] under the [[eye]], caused by lack of sleep, drug addiction etc.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2013|author=Ken Ilgunas|title=Walden on Wheels: On the Open Road from Debt to Freedom|page=14|passage=With gravel stuck to my cheek, I pulled myself back in the car, looked in the rearview mirror, and saw, looking back at me, a young man with a pale face and a purple '''bag''' under each eye. I looked pitiful {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|slang}} A small envelope that contains drugs, especially narcotics.
# {{c|en|Thousand}}{{lb|en|MLE|slang}} [[£]]1000, a [[grand]].
#* {{quote-song|en|title=Money Right|author=Figure Flows ft. Purple|album=Big Figures|date=2017-05-02|note=from 1:18|passage=Coulda got a '''bag''' last year<br/>But now I get a '''bag''' for a verse}}
# {{lb|en|informal}} A large number or amount.

